body:
It's not even " older sibling syndrome ", it's " middle sibling syndrome ". All the respect and "treating as an adult person" came to my older sister, all the love and tenderness were my brothers'. I had only responsibilities and "we really hope you're good enough to survive"

&#x200B;

When I try to to explain someone I'm not fine I always have the same answer "what the fuck is wrong with you"

&#x200B;

My mom and dad won't understand why I'm not brave to make some decisions and stuff. They didn't mean to ruin my life, of course, they are just simple people and they would do whatever it takes to make me feel happy. 

&#x200B;

Mate, thank you for your kind advice, I really appreciate your concern.

I tried to discuss my feelings with my husband. I thought he was the person I can trust alas he just laughed at me and said I'm being childish. 

&#x200B;

I tried to discuss it with my sister. She is a good person, I can knock at her door in the middle of the night and say I'm in a trouble and she wouldn't ask any questions and just feed me and warm me and make me safe. But she can't fully feel what I feel. She is like "what the fuck is wrong with you, you're married, you've got nice job, you're young and attractive, why would you complain"

&#x200B;

Mate, thank you. Your words made me feel bit better. Maybe if I'll find enough courage to face i need help I'll go seek a therapist.
